{"B_expression":"-1/(2*(1+u)**3*(sqrt(1+r/(1+u)**2)+1)**2)","C_expression":"-1/(2*(1+u))","derivation":"Retain the submitted program. The draft execution confirms exact algebraic cancellation: all rows inside the chi support (|r|<=1/4, |u|<=1/8) show residuals at machine-epsilon level (~1e-71), versus ~1e-4 for the linear reference. The single out-of-support row (r=-1.0, LEFT:x=1/8:s=0) correctly receives the bare r/2 increment and retains its 0.25 residual, as designed. All initial rows have u=0 so only B is active; the C=-1/(2(1+u)) term will engage once z departs from 1 in later field stages. The formula (1+u+g)^2=(1+u)^2+r is exact, verified symbolically via (s-1)(s+1)=r/(1+u)^2 with s=sqrt(1+r/(1+u)^2). Smoothness on an open neighbourhood of the closed rectangle |r|<=1/2,|u|<=1/4 follows from 1+u>=3/4 and 1+r/(1+u)^2>=7/9, keeping the square-root argument strictly positive.","inspect":[],"note":"Program retained unchanged. Successor should watch: (1) C term activates when stored z shifts from 1 (u!=0) after stage 1; (2) the r=-1.0 LEFT row is structurally outside chi_r and will always receive only r/2; (3) no analytic certificate has been issued but the expression is C-infinity on the required domain; (4) the source-only formula B(r)=-1/(2(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) is recovered at u=0, confirming consistency with the prior R1 derivation."}